<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI25-LINT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI25-LINT-001" ;
  triage:title "RULE-002 function-length hard violation: serve_runtime_scope grew to 80 lines, overlaps current diff" ;
  triage:description """CI job "Just lint (windows-latest)" on PR #640 (run 30202162750, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/actions/runs/30202162750/job/89793865090) failed at the `function-length` lint step with: "RULE-002 failed: new hard violations (80+ lines) overlap the current diff: crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs:404-483: serve_runtime_scope (80 lines)". This was introduced by commit a00e27ae916eaead45df6b610880d3537b2368a2 ("fix(ai25): bound peer reload and reconciliation"), which threaded a new `reload_runtime_view` generic parameter/closure through `serve_runtime_scope` and several callees to fix AI25-RSH-004 (moving the lifecycle reload off the accept-loop thread onto the dedicated lifecycle waiter thread). The function-length check was run locally against a fresh clone of feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution at commit a00e27ae916eaead45df6b610880d3537b2368a2, using `python3 scripts/check-function-length.py` (base ref origin/develop, confirmed by direct execution) -- confirmed reproducible outside CI, not a flaky/platform-specific failure (base threshold DEFAULT_FAIL_THRESHOLD=80, DEFAULT_WARN_THRESHOLD=70, defined in scripts/check-function-length.py). All other lint categories (fmt, clippy, deny, shear, version, boundaries, unix-gating, same-host-portability, runtime-waits, manifests, silent-emit, legacy-mailbox-paths, capability-degradation, identities, env-var-boundary, fixed-sleep, ttl-triage, lines, spell, daemon-singleton, pytests) passed on this same commit/job. Clippy, Format check, and all 3 Test legs (ubuntu/macos/windows) passed independently on run 30202162750. Just lint (macos-latest) and Just lint (ubuntu-latest) were still pending at triage time (Just lint checks run the exact same cross-platform-agnostic Python script, so they are expected to fail identically once they complete, but this is not yet confirmed). highest_open_branch determination: AICH-S5 (order 25) is the highest sprint with an active branch, and this defect is native to that branch's own commit (not present on any lower branch); highest_open_branch = feature/pAI-s25-peer-authority-resolution.""" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T13:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S5 ;
